# What the build context must not carry.
#
# A built checkout is several gigabytes, almost all of it output that the image
# rebuilds anyway (see packaging/container/Dockerfile). Everything listed here is
# generated; no tracked file matches any of these patterns.
#
# This belongs at the root of the build context, not next to the Dockerfile.
# BuildKit does read a "<dockerfile>.dockerignore" sibling, but only while the
# Dockerfile lies inside the context; where that does not hold it falls back
# here without warning, and a build that silently carries the whole tree costs
# gigabytes of context and picks up stale binaries.

.git
.github

# Compiler output. Not "lib/": the directory itself is tracked (via
# lib/.empty_file) because the makefiles copy into it without creating it, and
# excluding it makes the build fail in ClientServer.
**/*.o
**/*.a
**/*.dep

# The kernel and the client/server programs
bin/SecondoBDB
bin/SecondoCS
bin/SecondoListener
bin/SecondoMonitor
bin/SecondoRegistrar
bin/SecondoCheckpoint
bin/KeyValueStore

# Runtime artifacts of a local run: the monitor, the TTY and the persistent
# nested list all write relative to their working directory.
bin/tmp/
bin/temp_nested_list*/
**/temp_nested_list/
bin/server.msg
bin/proglogt.csv
bin/*.log
bin/.secondo_history
.secondo_history

# WebUI: the frontend bundle, its dependencies, the backend virtualenv and the
# pybind11 module are all rebuilt in the image.
**/node_modules/
**/.venv/
WebUI/frontend/dist/
WebUI/backend/native/*.so

# The packaging metadata is not part of the build. Excluding it also keeps the
# Dockerfile itself out of the context, so editing it does not invalidate the
# `COPY . /opt/secondo` layer and force a half-hour recompile. The entrypoint
# is the one file the runtime stage copies from the context, so it stays.
packaging/
!packaging/container/docker-entrypoint.sh

Algebras/Cassandra/tools/dsecondo-gui/target/
